<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila firm buys U.S. wheat, soybean.</title>
<headline>Manila firm buys U.S. wheat, soybean.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Philippine flour mill has bought 22,000 tonnes of U.S. wheat and 15,000 tonnes of soybeans for August delivery, traders said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Traders said the firm bought the spring wheat with 14 percent protein content at $3.82 per bushel FOB and the soybeans at $7.52 per bushel FOB.</p>
<p>The purchase was made on Friday night, traders involved in the deal said.</p>
<p>--Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8936, Fax 817-6267</p>
